  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- Move `DeleteSetup`, including the operation and linked-setup deletion guards and undo snapshots, into `commands/setup_delete.rs` without changing behavior. Preserve `commands::DeleteSetup` and `commands::setup::DeleteSetup`; keep the shared stock snapshot internal to commands.\r\n- Pin a generated linked child's toolpath becoming stale when its parent's alignment moves it, fresh again after one undo without regeneration, and stale after redo.\r\n- Remove the stray blank line in `commands/setup_align.rs` and record the bounded decision in `docs/decisions/398-setup-delete-staleness.md`.\r\n\r\n`commands/setup.rs` is now 335 lines (from 445); the deletion module is 124 lines.\r\n\r\n## Pinning and preservation\r\n\r\n`a_parent_alignment_makes_a_linked_childs_toolpath_stale_and_undo_restores_it` uses the real link, activate, create, generate and history commands. It first proves the operation belongs to the linked child and has a nonempty fresh path. A parent quarter-turn must move the child's alignment and a transformed part corner while leaving the square stock's shape/location unchanged, then report `Stale`; undo restores placement and `Ok`, and redo restores `Stale`.\r\n\r\nIndependent static review compared the complete moved `DeleteSetup` definition with the base: equal after whitespace normalization, including refusal order/messages, furniture ownership, removal and restoration. No actionable findings. Existing setup tests are retained; exactly one regression was added. No production transform/stamp, safety gate, schema or dependency change.\r\n\r\nReadings: issue #398 and its thread; current `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `docs/decisions/README.md`; setup command/alignment/relative, history and operation-stamp code and existing setup fixtures. No vendor implementation or assets consulted.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nNative Windows verification on this PR's exact tree, based on `37eacee3c7431ffd05783d84f38b7d18ad8dd623`:\r\n\r\n- Exact new regression: **1 passed**.\r\n- `scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -Base 37eacee3c7431ffd05783d84f38b7d18ad8dd623`: **870 passed, 0 failed, 8 ignored**, two steps, exit 0 (app 818; mapped UI integration 52).\r\n- All eight app `setup*.rs` suites: **58 passed**. Seven ran in quick; the omitted `setup_defines_wcs` ran separately (**4 passed**). These counts overlap the quick/regression results and are not additive.\r\n- `cargo clippy --locked -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: exit 0.\r\n- New-module Rust 2024 rustfmt check and base-to-tree `git diff --check`: exit 0.\r\n\r\nThe committed tree matches the independently reviewed and verified tree. Current-main integration preview is clean; no unrelated main advance was folded into the tested candidate.\r\n\r\nNot exercised: full release/heavy lanes (8 ignored in quick), Linux/macOS, manual UI or CNC. Internal UI setup-tree tests were not separately selected by the mapped gate. Graphify is unavailable, so source-level inspection was used. Hosted checks are intentionally absent under repository policy; no hosted CI-green claim.\r\n\r\nChangelog: none (behavior-preserving extraction and regression coverage).\r\n\r\nFixes #398\r\n",
